===================================================================================================
  HOW TO READ THIS — printed, not left to the reader
===================================================================================================
  ⛔ The margin column is INTERNAL: CRPS at the best bin count against CRPS at B=1, the
     unconditional empirical CDF of the same fit window. It is NOT the published −15.3% /
     −17.6%, which is against a PARAMETRIC emission and exists on months 457-469 alone.
  ⚠️ B* moved over 8000..16000 as the fit window moved over 13..36 months. A shorter fit window
     holds fewer members per bin, so a falling B* is the expected confound, not a finding
     against the method. Read B* beside the n/bin column, never alone.
  ⛔ SPLIT SENSITIVITY, NOT REPLICATION. One cube, one checkpoint, one seed, one family,
     one dropout rate, 49 months. Nothing here can see a defect common to all of them.
  ⛔ sb ONLY. The other two targets were discarded at cube-write time; the three-target
     half of #471 needs a new forward sweep, and #487 holds the decision about the writer.

